          "Spread the sample across the period, including busy weeks and thin coverage. Items drawn only from quiet weeks overstate the strength of the control. For each observation, record the time, reviewer, and source consulted. For a small population, state the count and uncertainty rather than a deceptive rate. A monthly sample reveals whether the rule survives a heavy week with partial coverage.",
