          "Changes in systems, policy, staffing, or account mix alter what a result means. Record those conditions beside the finding so its shelf life is clear. If a definition changes, show old and new rules side by side during the transition. Tag each item with the rule applied so comparisons stay fair. Escalate the pattern rather than the individual case when the same gap recurs.",
          "Study the distribution, not only the midpoint. A presentable median can conceal a long tail nobody has reviewed. State the number open and the age of the oldest item by owner. Together they reveal where work collects and which queue needs redesign. Record the reviewer and the time of the observation so a later question has somewhere to land. Record the reviewer and the time of the observation so a later question has somewhere to land."
